/-!
# The original marked root geometry in 14.7.73

The quotient construction retains S = ⟨Uᴸ⟩, the original k, E = S ∩ Sᵏ,
P = O₂(K), and the original qK. From marked image data it proves generation,
the core product, elementary abelianness of the literal P/E, its canonical
action, complementary root spaces and every projective recognition clause.
The universal G.1.3 implication then supplies natural copies. A one-copy
adapter constructs the required natural section and applies the existing
source quotient consumer.

The descendant `Geometry.Source` assembles the marked-image construction
and the chief-factor multiplicity argument from the genuine earlier setup
and 71/72 inputs, retaining only universal G.1.3 recognition beyond them.
It supplies the canonical projective quotient and the actual natural section,
with E = C_P(U). Import that descendant for the assembled conditional branch;
the parabolic/counting clauses and full 14.7.73 remain with the parent.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
14.7.73, printed pp.1076–1077 (PDF pp.1093–1094).
-/
